td {} [:a {:href "/events/92978"} "39 from 17 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Deaf fencer " [:a {:href "/athletes/20753"} "Ildikó Rejtő-Ujlaky"] " had been a regular on the international scene for nearly a decade but did not make her breakthrough as an individual until she claimed victory at the 1963 World Championships. She survived a close call in the quarter-finals where she needed a barrage but then proceeded to the final pool, defeating reigning Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/20718"} "Heidi Schmid"] " on the way.\nThe final pool stage proved inconclusive with Rejtő-Ujlaky, " [:a {:href "/athletes/20712"} "Helga Mees"] " of Germany and " [:a {:href "/athletes/20794"} "Antonella Ragno"] " of Italy each recording two wins out of three. Ragno lost both matches in the barrage which left the final match as Rejtő-Ujlaky versus Mees to decide the Olympic title. Mees had already defeated the Hungarian on two occasions during the competition but this time the tables were turned and Rejtő-Ujlaky emerged the winner by 4 hits to 2."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Rejtő-Ujlaky added a bronze medal in the individual event in 1968 and won team medals in every Olympic Games until 1976.\nAll three medallists were married to, or would later marry, fellow Olympians."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "106"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/20753"} "Ildikó Rejtő-Ujlaky"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "86"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/20712"} "Helga Mees"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style 